From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(client): inbound check-in for checks of single
 outbounds

A program on the router that checks a single outbound (internet-detector
with the check "sing-box outbound (Clash API)") gets only the delay from
the Clash API. Its other requests, such as the public IP, went through
sing-box by the routing rules, so their result was that of the route to
the requested host, not of the checked outbound.

The client config now has the inbound check-in: mixed on 127.0.0.1, port
infra.check_port (5334 by default, 0 - no inbound), one user per
outbound and endpoint (except block), the user name and password are its
tag. Rules at the start of the route send a connection of such a user
through its outbound, before all other rules. The inbound listens on
the loopback only; the other inbounds and rules are as before.

Checked with sing-box 1.14.3-extended ("sing-box check" of the config
generated from a real configuration; requests through check-in go out
through the outbound of the user, through mixed-in by the rules, a wrong
user or password is refused).

diff --git a/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc b/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc
index ef5be18..4cabea1 100755
--- a/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc
+++ b/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc
@@ -1281,6 +1281,37 @@ if (length(blocked_tags))
 			}
 		}
 
+/* Inbound for checks of single outbounds (internet-detector): mixed on
+ * 127.0.0.1, one user per outbound, the user name is its tag. A
+ * connection of that user goes through that outbound, before the routing
+ * rules. infra.check_port: the port, 0 - no such inbound. */
+const check_port = uci.get(uciconfig, uciinfra, 'check_port') || '5334';
+if (check_port !== '0') {
+	const check_tags = [];
+	for (let o in [...config.outbounds, ...(config.endpoints || [])])
+		if (o?.tag && o.type !== 'block' && !(o.tag in check_tags))
+			push(check_tags, o.tag);
+
+	if (length(check_tags)) {
+		push(config.inbounds, {
+			type: 'mixed',
+			tag: 'check-in',
+			listen: '127.0.0.1',
+			listen_port: int(check_port),
+			users: map(check_tags, (t) => ({ username: t, password: t }))
+		});
+		config.route.rules = [
+			...map(check_tags, (t) => ({
+				inbound: 'check-in',
+				auth_user: [t],
+				action: 'route',
+				outbound: t
+			})),
+			...config.route.rules
+		];
+	}
+}
+
 system('mkdir -p ' + RUN_DIR);
 
 /* With the evaluate and respond rules sing-box uses its new DNS rule mode,
